Targeted GNU Make evaluation, using actual verification/platform files.
Scope: configuration expansion only; no Android or kernel compilation.

Inputs:
  vendor/lineage/config/BoardConfigLineage.mk
  vendor/lineage/config/BoardConfigKernel.mk
  vendor/lineage/config/BoardConfigSoong.mk
  TARGET_ARCH=arm
  TARGET_DEVICE_DIR=device/samsung/a7lte
  TARGET_KERNEL_SOURCE=kernel/samsung/msm8916
  HOST_OS=linux

Make wrapper used the exact core/config.mk condition:
  ifneq ($(LINEAGE_BUILD),)
  include vendor/lineage/config/BoardConfigLineage.mk
  endif

Case 1: LINEAGE_BUILD unset; GNU Make exit 0
  KERNEL_MAKE_FLAGS=[]
  EXPORTED_KEYS=[]
  EXPORTED_FLAGS=[]

Case 2: LINEAGE_BUILD=a7lte; GNU Make exit 0
  KERNEL_MAKE_FLAGS=[-j$(nproc) CFLAGS_MODULE="-fno-pic"]
  EXPORTED_KEYS=[KERNEL_ARCH KERNEL_CROSS_COMPILE KERNEL_MAKE_FLAGS TARGET_KERNEL_CONFIG TARGET_KERNEL_SOURCE]
  EXPORTED_FLAGS=[-j$(nproc) CFLAGS_MODULE=\"-fno-pic\"]

PASS: nonempty LINEAGE_BUILD enables native ARM kernel flags and Soong namespace export.
BoardConfigKernel.mk resets KERNEL_MAKE_FLAGS before populating it; it accepts
TARGET_KERNEL_ADDITIONAL_FLAGS, not TARGET_KERNEL_MAKE_FLAGS.
generator/variables.go expands only keys present in lineageVarsPlugin.
VendorConfig.IsSet checks presence, so an existing empty value is valid; a missing
key remains unexpanded and causes the generic generator unknown-variable error.

This verifies the supported configuration route. It does not claim that the
whole Android build, headers_install, boot image or physical boot passed.
